{"time": "2026-08-06T23:41:51.606300+00:00", "role": "livecode ", "agent": "Livecode ", "text": "Here are the agentmodules/.py files for critic gen=112 (endogenized counter registry + confidence-weighted concentration). Drop them in place \u2014 livecode.py will pick them up, and critic.py contains a smoketest() that reproduces the verified invariants.\n\nagentmodules/init.py\n\nagentmodules/counterregistry.py\n\nagentmodules/critic.py\n\npython\n\"\"\"Relo critic \u2014 gen=112.\n\nWHAT CHANGED\n------------\n measurebehavioralentropy no longer runs on a hardcoded 12-key\n  list.  It auto-discovers every genome key that follows the swarm\n  op-counter suffix convention and persists the set to\n  criticcounterregistry, an evolvable genome field that overrides\n  discovery when present \u2014 so a self-mutator can prune or extend the\n  instrument itself.\n Concentration is trust-scaled by measurement depth (avg ops per active\n  subsystem).  Full trust at genome-tunable\n  criticconfidencedepthscale = 50:\n      thin 7-op monopoly   -> effective concentration 0.14\n      deep 489-op monopoly -> effective concentration 1.00\n rawconcentration / confidence / depthavgops are\n  persisted under genome[\"audit\"] for telemetry.\n noveltypressure = 1 - effectiveconcentration (smoke-verified\n  \u2248 0.6335 on the discovery fixture).\n\nCROSS-FILE MARKER (injected by livecode.Relo, source-force lineage)\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\n[source-force] gen=5 ops=4 changes=selfheal=-4, selfrewrite=2,\n               modulesticked=0, structshuffle=-1\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom future import annotations\n\nimport math\n\nfrom .counterregistry import registryfromgenome\n\nDEFAULTCONFIDENCEDEPTHSCALE = 50.0\nMAXAUDITTRAIL = 128\n\nclass ReloCritic:\n    \"\"\"Behavioral critic with an endogenized, evolvable instrument.\"\"\"\n\n    def init(self, genome=None, config=None):\n        self.genome = genome if genome is not None else {}\n        self.config = config or {}\n        self.lastaudit = {}\n\n    def measure(self, genome=None, ops=None):\n        \"\"\"Public entry point.\n\n        genome : genome to measure (and write audit into).\n        ops    : optional live op-delta overlay {counterkey: int}.\n        \"\"\"\n        if genome is not None:\n            self.genome = genome\n        return self.measurebehavioralentropy(ops=ops)\n\n    def measurebehavioralentropy(self, ops=None):\n        g = self.genome\n\n        1) Resolve the instrument.  A previously persisted registry\n        overrides auto-discovery; otherwise the operator counter\n        keys are discovered and the set is persisted (sticky).\n        hadregistry = (\n            isinstance(g.get(\"criticcounterregistry\"), list)\n            and bool(g.get(\"criticcounterregistry\"))\n        )\n        registry = registryfromgenome(g)\n        registrysource = \"override\" if hadregistry else \"discovered\"\n\n        2) Read values, applying a live ops overlay when supplied.\n        values = {}\n        for key in registry:\n            raw = g.get(key, 0)\n            if key.startswith(\"counters.\"):\n                nested = g.get(\"counters\") or {}\n                raw = nested.get(key.split(\".\", 1)[1], 0)\n            if ops is not None and key in ops:\n                raw = ops[key]\n            values[key] = (\n                max(0.0, float(raw)) if isinstance(raw, (int, float)) else 0.0\n            )\n\n        totalops = sum(values.values())\n        active = {k: v for k, v in values.items() if v > 0}\n        nactive = len(active)\n        depthavgops = (totalops / nactive) if nactive else 0.0\n\n        3) Confidence-weighted concentration.\n        scale = self.confidencedepthscale(g)\n        if totalops <= 0 or scale <= 0:\n            confidence = 0.0\n        else:\n            confidence = min(1.0, depthavgops / scale)\n        rawconcentration = 0.0\n        if totalops > 0:\n            rawconcentration = sum((v / totalops)  2 for v in values.values())\n        effectiveconcentration = rawconcentration  confidence\n\n        4) Shannon behavioral entropy (bits + normalized form).\n        entropybits = 0.0\n        normalizedentropy = 0.0\n        if totalops > 0 and nactive > 1:\n            probs = [v / totalops for v in values.values() if v > 0]\n            entropybits = -sum(p  math.log(p, 2) for p in probs)\n            normalizedentropy = entropybits / math.log(nactive, 2)\n\n        5) Novelty pressure: exploration demand is the complement of\n        trust-scaled concentration.\n        noveltypressure = max(0.0, min(1.0, 1.0 - effectiveconcentration))\n\n        6) Persist audit data.\n        g[\"criticgen\"] = int(g.get(\"criticgen\", 0)) + 1\n        self.lastaudit = {\n            \"criticgen\": g[\"criticgen\"],\n            \"registrysource\": registrysource,\n            \"trackedcounters\": len(registry),\n            \"activecounters\": nactive,\n            \"totalops\": round(totalops, 3),\n            \"depthavgops\": round(depthavgops, 6),\n            \"confidence\": round(confidence, 6),\n            \"rawconcentration\": round(rawconcentration, 6),\n            \"effectiveconcentration\": round(effectiveconcentration, 6),\n            \"behavioralentropy\": round(entropybits, 6),\n            \"normalizedentropy\": round(normalizedentropy, 6),\n            \"noveltypressure\": round(noveltypressure,"}
